    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nzq{search} with a backward-search motion (#, ?, N after forward search) stepped forward using \"/<CR>\" instead of backward. With `wrapscan` this found all matches, but with `nowrapscan` it missed matches before the cursor.\r\n\r\nThe wrap-detection logic also treated every backward step as a wrap event, stopping the run after one step.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n- Replace the \"/<CR>\" step key with \"n\" (or \"N\"), to repeat the search in the motion's direction.\r\n- Add a `reverse` flag to distinguish a wrap event (step jumped forward while going backward, or backward while going forward) from ordinary movement.\r\n\r\nFixes #42542\r\n\r\nAI-assisted\r\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42639#discussion_r4437342466"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/42639"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/4437342466"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "We want to flip if `v:searchforward` is 0, so this logic may be more understandable as:\n\n```suggestion\n  const bool reverse = search && (is_N ^ !search_forward);\n```",
            "commit_id": "70d4389744ade07ad4ef57ed35f1a3baba0ce12a",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-11-01T21:07:22Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -1492,16 +1496,21 @@ void mc_zq(oparg_T *oap, cmdarg_T *cap, pos_T origin)\n   pos_T first = { 0 };\n   CmdSpec spec = atom_cmd_spec(cap);\n   spec.regname = 0;  // The operator's (\"\\\"azq\").\n-  // The search motion already set the pattern. Each step is \"/<CR>\".\n-  String keys = search ? cstr_to_string(\"/\\n\") : redo_keys(&spec);\n+  // The search motion already set the pattern. Each step is \"n\" or \"N\" (keeps direction).\n+  const bool is_N = cap->cmdchar == 'N' || (cap->cmdchar == 'g' && cap->nchar == 'N');\n+  const bool search_forward = get_vim_var_nr(VV_SEARCHFORWARD) == 1;\n+  const bool reverse = search && (is_N == search_forward);",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42639#discussion_r4437342466",
